🏠 1. DASHBOARD (Home Page)
🎯 Purpose:

Quick overview of system health

👀 Viewer POV

Sees:

Total servers online
Avg CPU / RAM
Active alerts count
Server cards (status)
Live updates

👉 Use case:

“Is everything okay right now?”

👑 Admin POV

Same as viewer +:

Quick alert summary
Deployment status (later)
Quick actions (restart server, etc.)
🔥 Features
KPI cards
Server cards
Critical highlight
Live updates (Socket.io)
🖥️ 2. SERVERS PAGE
🎯 Purpose:

Manage + inspect servers

👀 Viewer POV
List of all servers
Status (online/offline)
Basic metrics
Click → detailed view

👉 Use case:

“Which server is acting weird?”

👑 Admin POV

Everything above +:

➕ Add new server
❌ Remove server
✏️ Edit server details
Enable/disable monitoring
Tag servers (prod/dev)
🔥 Features
Server list table
Search + filter
Status badges
Actions column (admin only)
🚨 3. ALERTS PAGE
🎯 Purpose:

Central alert management

👀 Viewer POV
View active alerts
Filter (critical / warning)
See history of alerts
Click → view details

👉 Use case:

“What’s broken right now?”

👑 Admin POV

Everything above +:

✅ Resolve alert manually
🔧 Configure thresholds
🔔 Set alert rules
📧 Email notification config
🔥 Features
Alert list (active + resolved)
Severity filter
Timeline
Acknowledge/resolve button
📈 4. HISTORY PAGE
🎯 Purpose:

Analyze past performance

👀 Viewer POV
Select server
View CPU/RAM/Disk charts
Time filters (1h / 24h / 7d)

👉 Use case:

“When did things go wrong?”

👑 Admin POV

Everything above +:

Export data (CSV/PDF)
Compare servers
Deep analytics
🔥 Features
Charts (Chart.js)
Server dropdown
Time range filter
Trend analysis
